tool_definition.description:
Executes a search with the exact query string provided. Pass the user’s query verbatim via the single parameter "query". Do not edit, reorder, trim, normalize, escape, URL-encode, quote, or otherwise transform the string. Preserve all characters exactly as given, including spaces (even multiple), punctuation, case, diacritics, and search operators (e.g., site:, inurl:, quotes, AND/OR, parentheses). Token order matters. Only include the key "query"; no additional parameters.
Parameter:
- query (string, required): The exact search query to submit, unchanged.
Returns: The most relevant results for that exact query.
Examples:
- Correct: {"query":"site:docs.github.com \"Actions cache\" path:/en/enterprise"}
- Incorrect (reordered): {"query":"path:/en/enterprise site:docs.github.com Actions cache"}
- Incorrect (wrong key): {"q":"..."}
- Incorrect (added quoting): {"query":"'site:example.com test'"}
